rage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F2fd89102-b824-4df8-abe9-b9abd3157e9b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 388px; height: 248px;\" /></p><p>A zwitterion is a compound with no overall electrical charge, but which contains separate parts which are positively and negatively charged.</p><p>Sulphanilic acid exist as dipolar ion (zwitter ion); act as inner salt and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> group diminishes the basic character of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"BITSAT 2019","_marksId":"64c0e8066f5bfc7ab78ae9ed"},{"id":17291,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"The most reactive amine towards reactions with dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PhNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>More be the ability of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>-atom of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> group to donate lone pair of electrons to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> (dil.), more be the reactivity of amine.</p><p>In (B) two alkyl groups are attached to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> (having electron releasing nature) which increases the electron donating ability of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>-atom of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. In aqueous medium, secondary amine is most basic. Hence, it is most reactive. In (D), due to resonance, lone pair of electrons get delocalised and its basic strength is very less.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"BITSAT 2017","_marksId":"64c0e7ea6f5bfc7ab78ae8f5"},{"id":17292,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"<p>In the reaction, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mover><mo>⟶</mo><mi>KCN</mi></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>⟶</mo><msub><mi>LiAlH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math> end product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math> is</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2<